cool breeze <nochsfentor@yahoo.com> wrote:
> I had a recent wizard, and he found a dwarvish mithril coat not far
> into the dungeon. Putting it on, I found his spell casting to be quite
> bad.  Now, as I understand from looking at some of the spoilers that
> elven mithril coat does not hamper spellcasting and even provides some
> resistances to enemy spellcasting.  My question is, is this early
> dwarven mithril coat just something to drop in a general store or is
> there some use for this usually powerful item?

If your spoiler really says that elven mithril-coat doesn't hamper
spellcasting it is plain wrong. Mithril is metallic and all metal
armor affect spellcasting.

The other bit also doesn't seem to be correct. Mithril-coat gives you
the highest possible protection of magic-cancellation, but that
doesn't mean you have any protection of magic monster spells.
http://nethackwiki.com/wiki/Magic_cancellation


Usually for an early game wizard, more AC beats spellcasting. An early
wizard is rather weak as spellcaster and so you should keep your
dwarvish mithril-coat until you've got enough PW and XP for good
spellcasting.

